// BT-3841 (ADR 0131): a plain `detect:` whose block writes an outer local, in
// the REPL. As a statement it keeps the REPL's own lowering and stops at the
// first match (BT-3805). In a conditional arm it leaks the fold's tuple and
// drops the write (measured, PR 5), so the Phase 0 check keeps rejecting it
// there (the REPL arm rows are unmeasured, BT-3823). `detect:ifNone:` in the
// same arm answers right and keeps its writes (last cases).

t := 0
// => 0

#(1, 2) detect: [:e | t := t + 1. e > 0]
// => 1

t
// => 1

#(1, 2) detect: [:e | t := t + e. e > 1]
// => 2

t
// => 4

4 =:= 4 ifTrue: [#(1, 2) detect: [:e | t := t + 1. e > 0]]
// => ERROR: `detect:` writes outer local `t`, but as a statement inside a conditional arm

4 =:= 4 ifTrue: [#(1, 2) detect: [:e | t := t + 1. e > 0] ifNone: [0]]
// => 1

t
// => 5

4 =:= 4 ifTrue: [#(1, 2) detect: [:e | e > 5] ifNone: [t := t + 100. 0]]
// => 0

t
// => 105
